      "message": "If \"run\" is truly a no-op, I\"m fine with leaving it as unset, but I think that we best not have it as a no-op if we\u0027re using the `command` structure. As it stands in your CL, we\u0027re only adding it as a command so that we can initialize config and context objects, but really we are otherwise ignoring the `command` structure -- this is a bit of a \"code smell\"; in general, we should avoid making \"fake values\" or half-empty values to meet an API need -- it\u0027s an indication that the API needs to be refactored or re-evaluated,",
